  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the mirror image $Q$ when the point $P(2,5)$ is reflected in the line $2x+3y=6$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$Q(-2,-1)$.\n\nThe perpendicular meets the mirror line at $M(0,2)$; repeat the displacement from $P$ to $M$.",
      "worked": "The mirror line is $y=-\\frac23x+2$, so the perpendicular gradient is $\\frac32$. The perpendicular through $P$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}y-5&=\\frac32(x-2)\\\\y-5&=\\frac32x-3\\\\y&=\\frac32x+2.\\end{align*}$$\nAt its intersection $M$ with the mirror line,\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+3\\left(\\frac32x+2\\right)&=6\\\\\\frac{13}{2}x+6&=6\\\\\\frac{13}{2}x&=0\\\\x&=0\\\\y&=\\frac32(0)+2\\\\y&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $M(0,2)$. From $P$ to $M$ the displacement is two units left and three units down. Repeat this displacement from $M$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x_Q&=0-2=-2\\\\y_Q&=2-3=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $Q(-2,-1)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 148
  },
